# Quality

Run commands from the repo root. There is no CI workflow and no frontend test target. Do not report a check you did not run.

- `admin`: `pnpm exec nx lint admin`, `pnpm exec nx format-check admin`, `pnpm exec nx typecheck admin`
- `customer`: `pnpm exec nx lint customer`, `pnpm exec nx format-check customer` (no `typecheck` target)
- `api`: `pnpm exec nx format-check api`, `pnpm exec nx vet api`, `pnpm exec nx test api`

`pnpm exec nx format <project>` writes fixes. Format-check only reports drift.

## Tools

- Oxlint lints `admin` and `customer` (`--deny-warnings` in each `project.json`). It does not lint Go.
- Prettier (single quotes, semicolons, trailing commas, print width 100) formats the frontends. `.prettierignore` excludes `apps/api`.
- Go format and checks are `gofmt`, `go vet`, and `go test` through the `api` targets. `format-check` runs `gofmt -l cmd internal` and exits 1 when files differ. `.editorconfig` sets spaces for every file; `gofmt` still owns `*.go` and uses tabs.
- `apps/api/internal` is empty and untracked. `format-check` fails if that directory is missing.

## Hooks

`.husky/pre-commit` runs admin/customer lint, format-check for all three projects, and `pnpm exec nx vet api`. Each step ends with `|| exit 1`. Keep that failure behavior. The hook checks whole projects, not the Git index, and does not run tests.

`.husky/commit-msg` runs Commitlint with `@commitlint/config-conventional`.

If staged-file tooling is added, leave unstaged changes untouched and still exit nonzero when a check fails.

## Environment

`.gitignore` ignores `.env` and `.env.*`, then un-ignores `.env.example`. Commit only example files, with local placeholders and no live secrets.

- Admin: `VITE_API_BASE_URL`
- Customer: `API_BASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`
- API: `PORT`, `DATABASE_URL`, `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`
